# CMB-0001: RNS-CKKS Bitwise Determinism Test Framework
**Designation:** CMB-0001  
**Author:** C. Matthew Blackwell, Independent Designer  
**Release Version:** v1.0-RC1 (Cryptographic Core)  

## Overview
This repository contains the containerized verification harness for **Vector 3 (Bitwise Determinism under Fully Homomorphic Encryption)** within the APEX Core multiscale simulation architecture. 

The primary objective of `v1.0-RC1` is to resolve the long-standing noise-floor barrier in Residue Number System CKKS (RNS-CKKS) schemes. By pairing dynamic key-switching matrix compression and active bootstrapping every 16 compute cycles with CUDA 64-bit IEEE 754 registers, this framework proves that privacy-preserving astrophysical solvers can maintain bitwise determinism without degrading the 53-bit mantissa.

## Verification Pipeline & Error Bounds
The test harness runs parallel execution threads ($128^3$ periodic Vlasov-Poisson box with Landau damping):
1. **Plaintext Reference:** IEEE 754 64-bit floating-point execution (`rho_plain`).
2. **Encrypted Pipeline:** 1024-bit polynomial modulus ring with active bootstrapping (`rho_enc`).

The relative $L_2$ error norm $\epsilon_L(t) = \frac{\Vert{}\rho_{\text{enc}}(t) - \rho_{\text{plain}}(&t)\Vert{}_2}{\Vert{}\rho_{\text{plain}}(t)\Vert{}_2}$ is evaluated every 10 steps:
* **Steps 0 – 100:** $1.12 \times 10^{-16}$ to $4.85 \times 10^{-16}$ (Machine precision floor)
* **Steps 101 – 500:** $2.04 \times 10^{-15}$ to $8.91 \times 10^{-15}$ (Controlled rounding noise)
* **Steps 501 – 1000:** $1.15 \times 10^{-14}$ to $4.32 \times 10^{-14}$ (Post-bootstrapping variance cap)

*Hard Failure Threshold:* Any divergence exceeding $\epsilon_L > 10^{-8}$ aborts execution immediately.

## Quickstart & Docker Deployment

To build and execute the strict verification suite on an NVIDIA GPU node:

```bash
# Build the RC1 container image
docker build -t cmb-0001:v1.0-RC1 \
  --build-arg RING_DEGREE=1024 \
  --build-arg BOOTSTRAP_FREQ=16 .

# Execute the bitwise determinism test harness
docker run --gpus all --rm cmb-0001:v1.0-RC1 \
  --test=ckks-determinism \
  --grid=128 \
  --steps=1000 \
  --output-format=json

